      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Hardcoding `.ahb4` here in the generic `core/cortex-m/init.S` will break the build for almost all other Cortex-M boards. \n\n`__ahb4_start` and `__ahb4_end` are only generated by the linker script if the `.ahb4` region is explicitly defined (which is currently only true for `CHIP_VARIANT_STM32H7X3` in `chip/stm32/memory_regions.inc`). For all other Cortex-M boards (e.g., using NPCX, ITE, or other STM32 families), the linker will fail with an `undefined reference to \u0027__ahb4_start\u0027` error.\n\n**Remediation Options:**\n1. **Conditional Compilation:** Wrap this initialization block (including the symbol definitions at the bottom of the file) in `#ifdef CHIP_VARIANT_STM32H7X3` (or a new generic Kconfig like `CONFIG_HAS_AHB4_SRAM`).\n2. **Weak Symbols:** Declare `__ahb4_start` and `__ahb4_end` as `.weak` in this file. If the symbols are undefined, they will resolve to `0`, making `_ahb4_start \u003d\u003d _ahb4_end` and safely skipping the loop.\n3. **Chip-Specific Init:** Move this initialization out of the generic architecture startup code and into a chip-specific initialization hook that runs early in the boot process.",
